{"name":"Rum Raisin","hex":"#683b3c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2/B language code for Romanian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spirit distilled from various preparations of sugarcane, particularly fermented cane sugar and molasses.","A serving of rum."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rum"},{"term":"raisin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dried grape."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Of fruit: to dry out; to become like raisins.","To flavor (an alcoholic beverage) with fruit that has raisined."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raisin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rum raisin","blocks":[{"text":"Rum raisin is an ice cream flavor prepared with a combination of rum, raisins and vanilla ice cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/MOW_PRIME_Gold_Rum_Raisin_-_2.jpg/330px-MOW_PRIME_Gold_Rum_Raisin_-_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rum_raisin"},{"title":"Rum","blocks":[{"text":"Rum is a liquor made by fermenting and then distilling sugarcane molasses or sugarcane juice. The distillate, initially a clear liquid, is often aged in barrels. Rum originated in the Caribbean in the 17th century, where it was likely first created by enslaved people on sugar plantations, but has come to be produced in nearly every major sugar-producing region of the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/A_glass_of_rum.jpg/330px-A_glass_of_rum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rum"},{"title":"Raisin","blocks":[{"text":"A raisin is a dried grape. Raisins are produced in many regions of the world and may be eaten raw or used in cooking, baking, and brewing. The word raisin is commonly used for the dried dark-colored seedless grape, while sultana is a golden-colored dried grape, and currant is a dried small Black Corinth seedless grape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Raisins_01.jpg/330px-Raisins_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raisin"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg/500px-Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg/1280px-Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg/500px-Rum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rum display in a liquor store (United States, 2009)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARum_display_in_liquor_store.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Government_house_rum.jpg/500px-Government_house_rum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Government_house_rum.jpg/1280px-Government_house_rum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Government_house_rum.jpg/500px-Government_house_rum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Government House rum, manufactured by the Virgin Islands Company distillery in Saint Croix, circa 1941","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGovernment_house_rum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Mount_Gay_Rum_Visitors_Centre%2C_Spring_Garden_HWY%2C_Barbados-002.jpg/500px-Mount_G